WEBVTT

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.920
Morgan opens Harbor's paper planning

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:03.180
folder on Friday.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.160
The Session Option Brief is still held

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:07.230
because no one has confirmed staffing.

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:09.810
An idea appears in the margin: perhaps a

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:11.310
different brief format would make the

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:12.300
next review easier.

00:00:12.676 --> 00:00:16.900
It is tempting to let the preparation agent change the format and declare an improvement.

00:00:17.327 --> 00:00:23.343
But Harbor has no baseline for review time, no test plan, and no permission to change the team's process.

00:00:23.979 --> 00:00:26.198
The honest first artifact is a proposal.

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:33.792
Chapter Twenty-Three separates five states: propose, not run, gate, trace, then approve or discard.

00:00:34.449 --> 00:00:41.531
For the Harbor case, the proposed question is narrow: would a brief that puts staffing evidence first help Morgan identify a hold faster?

00:00:42.257 --> 00:00:44.689
The hypothesis needs a comparison and a metric.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:48.121
We could compare two course brief layouts in a paper exercise.

00:00:48.846 --> 00:00:52.004
We cannot claim one works better because it looks cleaner to us.

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:55.887
The `not_run` state records exactly what is missing.

00:00:56.587 --> 00:01:08.278
The workbook's AutoResearch Proposal asks for the baseline, experiment configuration, expected impact, touched settings, metric gate, risk, rollback, approval question, and next gate.

00:01:08.747 --> 00:01:10.838
Here the baseline is `unknown`, not zero.

00:01:11.577 --> 00:01:18.020
The proposed metric is whether a reviewer correctly identifies the staffing hold, with time to find it as a secondary observation.

00:01:18.617 --> 00:01:19.769
No result exists yet.

00:01:20.239 --> 00:01:22.713
The touched surface would be the paper brief layout only.

00:01:23.417 --> 00:01:25.593
The rollback is to keep the current layout.

00:01:25.891 --> 00:01:29.646
No routing default, memory record, or real calendar changes.

00:01:30.371 --> 00:01:34.339
Morgan owns the review of the proposal because Morgan owns this planning decision.

00:01:34.954 --> 00:01:40.629
A real experiment would need a fresh, scoped approval and an appropriate participant and privacy plan.

00:01:41.183 --> 00:01:42.719
This lesson grants none of that.

00:01:43.307 --> 00:01:50.048
In the paper scenario, Morgan can reject the idea, ask for a clearer baseline, or authorize a later bounded test.

00:01:50.688 --> 00:01:54.358
The agent cannot turn a promising hypothesis into durable memory.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:59.844
A memory proposal would need its own source, scope, expiry, and human decision.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:09.273
Write a `not_run` reason that another person can act on: `No agreed comparison set or reviewer protocol; staffing hold remains unresolved.`

00:02:09.927 --> 00:02:13.895
Then add the next safe step: Morgan reviews whether the question is worth testing at all.

00:02:14.279 --> 00:02:17.266
If Morgan says no, keep the rejection and its reason.

00:02:17.735 --> 00:02:21.063
If Morgan says yes, define the test before anyone runs it.

00:02:21.511 --> 00:02:24.071
Either path teaches Harbor something about its priorities.

00:02:24.583 --> 00:02:27.015
A silent queue of ideas teaches almost nothing.

00:02:27.655 --> 00:02:29.148
Pause on your own workflow type.

00:02:29.533 --> 00:02:32.306
What evidence would make your favorite improvement worth testing?

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:34.764
Draft one AutoResearch Proposal.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:48.801
Name the question, hypothesis, comparison, current baseline, primary metric and guardrail, expected direction, risk, touched surface, rollback, owner, approval question, and next metric gate.

00:02:49.447 --> 00:02:51.330
Mark the result `not_run`.

00:02:51.879 --> 00:02:55.549
Write the reason in plain language and the action Morgan may take after review.

00:02:56.189 --> 00:02:58.237
Keep the staffing and spend holds visible.

00:02:58.621 --> 00:03:00.455
Use a fictional or approved example.

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:53.025
Do not use private operational data, run a provider, contact anyone, change a setting, or promote a finding.

00:03:53.579 --> 00:03:55.414
Save revision thirteen as a draft.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:01.075
Research begins when a question can survive a gate, not when a dashboard fills with experiments.

00:04:01.797 --> 00:04:03.807
Harbor has a proposal that someone can

00:04:03.847 --> 00:04:06.157
inspect, and a clear record that nothing

00:04:06.327 --> 00:04:07.007
has run.
